<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth> a pk1:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Savin et al. (2011) discrete gut rod coupled to a finite-element (CST, St.Venant-Kirchhoff) dorsal-mesentery membrane with an apicobasal Pitx2 stiffness gradient (Vertebrate midgut & dorsal mesentery (Gallus gallus, Coturnix japonica, Taeniopygia guttata, Mus musculus))",
        "Savin et al. (2011) discrete gut rod coupled to a finite-element (CST, St.Venant-Kirchhoff) dorsal-mesentery membrane with an apicobasal Pitx2 stiffness gradient faithfully reproduces Vertebrate midgut & dorsal mesentery (Gallus gallus, Coturnix japonica, Taeniopygia guttata, Mus musculus) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Vertebrate midgut & dorsal mesentery (Gallus gallus, Coturnix japonica, Taeniopygia guttata, Mus musculus) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 80.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-gut-looping-differential-growth-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py> ;
    schema:about "Vertebrate midgut & dorsal mesentery (Gallus gallus, Coturnix japonica, Taeniopygia guttata, Mus musculus)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A Kirchhoff rod with twist, a Kirchhoff-Love shell, chirality / handedness selection, mesh-converged loop numbers, measured Pitx2 stiffness gradients, moduli for the BMP2/Noggin conditions traceable to Nerurkar 2017, or an embryonic-chick specimen image (the vendored photograph is an adult mammalian mesentery)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Analytical strain, annular inertia and cube-law predictions; a 96-node discrete rod (axial + second-difference bending energy) sharing its nodes with the gut edge of a 96 x 5 CST St.Venant-Kirchhoff plane-stress membrane mesh of a trapezoidal fan (root fixed, rod ends pinned) with a mean-preserving apicobasal Pitx2 stiffness field; L-BFGS-B relaxation with emergent turning-number loop count, R = 1/<kappa>, contour length per loop and tortuosity for E8-E16, BMP2/WT/Noggin/ablation at E12, a Pitx2-gradient sweep and a mesh-refinement check; the 14-point analytical collapse; chromaticity + DoG segmentation of a vendored mesentery photograph",
        "reported_in_source: Kurpios et al. (2008), Davis et al. (2008): Pitx2-dependent left-right asymmetric condensation and architecture of the dorsal mesentery set the handedness of looping",
        "reported_in_source: Nerurkar, Mahadevan & Tabin (2017): BMP2 over-expression increases and Noggin decreases the differential strain and the number of loops at E12",
        "reported_in_source: Savin et al. (2011): the midgut loops because the tube grows faster than the dorsal mesentery it is attached to (strain epsilon = (L_t - L_m)/L_m); loop wavelength and radius scale as lambda = 4.55 ell_*, R = 1.68 ell_* with ell_* = (E_t I_t / (E_m h_m))^(1/3); surgically freed tubes uncoil; the collapse holds across chick ontogeny (E8-E16) and across zebra finch, quail, chick and mouse (Fig. 4e-f)",
        "transfer_boundary: The 14-point cross-species table in gut_looping_differential_growth_reference.json reproduces lambda = 4.55 ell_* and R = 1.68 ell_* to ~1 % with identical log-log slopes for lambda and R, so the r = 0.9999 collapse is a consistency check of the table against the law, not an independent validation against digitised Fig. 4e-f data",
        "transfer_boundary: The FE model is a pure membrane (no sheet bending, no left-right rest curvature): looping handedness is NOT selected and the script makes no chirality claim; W_m/L_m = 0.18, root fraction 0.7, nu_m = 0.45 and a_Pitx2 = 0.4 are modelling assumptions flagged in fe_mesentery_mesh_reference.json, not measurements",
        "transfer_boundary: The emergent morphometrics are unfitted: E12 N = 9.81 vs 8.5, R = 0.952 vs 1.15 mm; E8-E16 MAPE 18.7 % (N) and 21.4 % (R); the ontogenetic log-log slope of R_sim vs ell_* is 0.61 (cube law 1.0); N changes by 7.7 % on 96x5 -> 128x6 refinement" ;
    pk1:aristotelianEfficientCause "7. Elastic Shell/Sheet Buckling" ;
    pk1:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPoionForm "Gyri, Villi, Loops & Snap-Shells" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPosonLaw "Wrinkling lambda ~ h(E_f/E_s)^1/3" ;
    pk1:aristotelianSubalternClass "Aves (Ornithes)" ;
    pk1:biologicalGenus "Gallus" ;
    pk1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py; output: docs/media/gut_looping_differential_growth_comparison.png; organism: Vertebrate midgut & dorsal mesentery (Gallus gallus, Coturnix japonica, Taeniopygia guttata, Mus musculus); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/327729c8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 6fb7e55e6158cd10ddf94728c17f791e81e999f808f135655cb2a64003d9cc1b; artifact_sha256: ecc65dee03e0c3a533d95c7271c0e853a30687d6ea5ba5c237d41f3e7f9c41e4; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/fe_mesentery_mesh_reference.json=8025ecf7fd54a0ef..., datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/gut_looping_differential_growth_reference.json=f73121bb4140187f..., datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/intestine_mesentery_specimen.jpg=e12fee9ac1fb5f3d..., datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/paper_citations.bib=201f4db588717f47..., datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/scout_manifest.json=0723b42b4d825087...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-gut-looping-differential-growth-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Savin et al. (2011): the midgut loops because the tube grows faster than the dorsal mesentery it is attached to (strain epsilon = (L_t - L_m)/L_m); loop wavelength and radius scale as lambda = 4.55 ell_*, R = 1.68 ell_* with ell_* = (E_t I_t / (E_m h_m))^(1/3); surgically freed tubes uncoil; the collapse holds across chick ontogeny (E8-E16) and across zebra finch, quail, chick and mouse (Fig. 4e-f) | Nerurkar, Mahadevan & Tabin (2017): BMP2 over-expression increases and Noggin decreases the differential strain and the number of loops at E12 | Kurpios et al. (2008), Davis et al. (2008): Pitx2-dependent left-right asymmetric condensation and architecture of the dorsal mesentery set the handedness of looping; reconstructed_in_script: Analytical strain, annular inertia and cube-law predictions; a 96-node discrete rod (axial + second-difference bending energy) sharing its nodes with the gut edge of a 96 x 5 CST St.Venant-Kirchhoff plane-stress membrane mesh of a trapezoidal fan (root fixed, rod ends pinned) with a mean-preserving apicobasal Pitx2 stiffness field; L-BFGS-B relaxation with emergent turning-number loop count, R = 1/<kappa>, contour length per loop and tortuosity for E8-E16, BMP2/WT/Noggin/ablation at E12, a Pitx2-gradient sweep and a mesh-refinement check; the 14-point analytical collapse; chromaticity + DoG segmentation of a vendored mesentery photograph; transfer_boundary: The FE model is a pure membrane (no sheet bending, no left-right rest curvature): looping handedness is NOT selected and the script makes no chirality claim; W_m/L_m = 0.18, root fraction 0.7, nu_m = 0.45 and a_Pitx2 = 0.4 are modelling assumptions flagged in fe_mesentery_mesh_reference.json, not measurements | The emergent morphometrics are unfitted: E12 N = 9.81 vs 8.5, R = 0.952 vs 1.15 mm; E8-E16 MAPE 18.7 % (N) and 21.4 % (R); the ontogenetic log-log slope of R_sim vs ell_* is 0.61 (cube law 1.0); N changes by 7.7 % on 96x5 -> 128x6 refinement | The 14-point cross-species table in gut_looping_differential_growth_reference.json reproduces lambda = 4.55 ell_* and R = 1.68 ell_* to ~1 % with identical log-log slopes for lambda and R, so the r = 0.9999 collapse is a consistency check of the table against the law, not an independent validation against digitised Fig. 4e-f data; does_not_claim: A Kirchhoff rod with twist, a Kirchhoff-Love shell, chirality / handedness selection, mesh-converged loop numbers, measured Pitx2 stiffness gradients, moduli for the BMP2/Noggin conditions traceable to Nerurkar 2017, or an embryonic-chick specimen image (the vendored photograph is an adult mammalian mesentery)]" ;
    pk1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2008.05.001>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature10277>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0803578105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1618677114>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1238842> ;
    pk1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-code-traceability>,
