<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Savin et al. (2011) discrete gut rod coupled to a finite-element (CST, St.Venant-Kirchhoff) dorsal-mesentery membrane with an apicobasal Pitx2 stiffness gradient — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module header (L1-66) maps Laws 1-5 to their Lean theorems and to Savin 2011 / Nerurkar 2017 / Kurpios 2008; the Section 3 header (L236-247) documents the Pass 3 mechanism, the boundary conditions and the limitations; every new function cites its equation or Lean theorem in its docstring (`build_fan_mesentery_mesh` L257-262, `pitx2_stiffness_field` L304-306, `relax_rod_fe_mesentery` L360-365); the math-KG YAML registers 5 equations with single-range `code_locus` pins. Deductions: `lambda_sim_mm` now equals contour length per loop L_t/N (L492-493), not Savin's lambda, but keeps the old key name used downstream (-4); `relax_kirchhoff_gut_rod` (L511) and the Section 3 title call a second-difference rod a 'Kirchhoff rod' (-3); the plane-stress Lame conversion (L390-391), the 0.02 W_m roughness amplitude (L407) and the n_r//10 interior trim (L460) carry no comment or source (-3); the Pass 2 remnants in the measurement names ('3D Kirchhoff rod') were renamed but the README of the dataset still describes the v2 solver in its earlier sections (-2); credit for the FD gradient check that makes the stated energy auditable." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py L490–L511: lambda_sim_mm aliased to contour_per_loop_sim_mm (not Savin's lambda); relax_kirchhoff_gut_rod alias is a misnomer for a second-difference rod <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py#L490-L511>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Savin et al. (2011) discrete gut rod coupled to a finite-element (CST, St.Venant-Kirchhoff) dorsal-mesentery membrane with an apicobasal Pitx2 stiffness gradient — Model fidelity to source: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The analytical core is Savin's (strain L170-175, annular inertia L178-184, ell_* and the 4.55 / 1.68 prefactors L187-205) and the Pass 3 mechanism is a genuine coupled rod + sheet energy: a trapezoidal fan triangulated into 760 CST elements (L251-300), a St.Venant-Kirchhoff plane-stress membrane embedded in 3D with the exact first-Piola gradient (L312-339), rod axial and bending terms assembled on the shared gut-edge nodes (L418-441), root fixed and rod ends pinned (L403-414), and emergent turning-number N, R = 1/<kappa> and tortuosity (L454-468). Nothing prescribes the loop shape, and E_m = 0 releases the rod to a straight configuration. Deductions: the sheet is a pure membrane with no bending stiffness or left-right rest curvature, so the handedness that Kurpios 2008 / Davis 2008 attribute to the mesentery is not selected and the model is silent on chirality (-6); the SVK membrane resists compression, so compressed sheet regions act as an unphysical foundation instead of wrinkling (acknowledged at L242-247) (-3); the rod bending energy is a second-difference penalty without twist, so 'Kirchhoff rod' in the alias L511 and the Section 3 header overstates it (-3); the emergent R exponent across E8-E16 is 0.61 instead of the cube law's 1.0 and R is 21 % low, i.e. the reduced model does not reproduce the paper's central scaling result from mechanics alone (-4); the ablation branch simply zeroes E_m and releases the ends rather than modelling a dissected sheet (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py L1566–L1574: Emergent R MAPE 0.214 across E8-E16 and log-log slope of R_sim vs ell_* = 0.61 (cube law 1.0): the reduced model does not reproduce the ontogenetic exponent <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py#L1566-L1574>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-model-fidelity-5> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Savin et al. (2011) discrete gut rod coupled to a finite-element (CST, St.Venant-Kirchhoff) dorsal-mesentery membrane with an apicobasal Pitx2 stiffness gradient — Morphometric validation: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1493-1645) returns 13 reference-anchored measurements, 6 of them new and all emergent: E12 N_sim = 9.81 (ref 8.5), R_sim = 0.952 mm (ref 1.15), E8-E16 R MAPE 0.214 with N MAPE 0.187 and the R exponent 0.61 in the note, Pitx2 dN/da = 0.68 loops per unit a, mesh sensitivity 0.077, membrane-gradient FD error 8.2e-11, ablation tortuosity 1.000, BMP2/Noggin ratio 2.93 (ref 2.09), plus the retained 4-species r = 0.9999 / alpha = 0.991 / lambda/R = 2.7065 and specimen CV. The honest disclosure of MAPE, exponent and mesh sensitivity is credited. Deductions: the headline validations fail at the 15-21 % level and the R exponent misses the cube law (-8); the 4-species Pearson r and alpha validate a table that is itself law-generated (see source-traceability), so three of the 13 measurements are circular (-6); the Pitx2 measurement has no quantitative reference (null hypothesis 0.0, L1576-1584) (-3); the BMP2/Noggin ratio moved from 1.86 to 2.93 against a reference of 2.09 and the per-condition N errors (14.65 vs 11.5, 4.99 vs 5.5) are not themselves measurements (-3); no uncertainty (seed ensemble or mesh pair) is attached to the emergent E12 N and R beyond the single refinement check (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py L1514–L1544: 4-species Pearson r, RMSE and log-log alpha computed against the cross_species_scaling table that reproduces the law to ~1 % (circular) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py#L1514-L1544>",
        "2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py L1576–L1584: Pitx2 dN/da reference is the null hypothesis 0.0 because no quantitative gradient is reported in Kurpios 2008 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py#L1576-L1584>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-measurement-4-species-gut-loop-radius-of-curvature-scaling-correlation-savin-et-al-2011-fig-4f>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-measurement-4-species-gut-loop-wavelength-scaling-correlation-savin-et-al-2011-fig-4e>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-measurement-biological-specimen-segmented-inter-loop-wavelength-cv-intestine-mesentery-specimen-jpg>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-measurement-bmp2-vs-noggin-loop-count-modulation-ratio-at-e12-nerurkar-et-al-2017-pnas>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-measurement-chick-e12-fe-coupled-rod-emergent-loop-count-n-sim-turning-number>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-measurement-chick-e12-fe-coupled-rod-emergent-loop-radius-r-sim-1-kappa>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-measurement-chick-e8-e16-emergent-loop-radius-mean-absolute-percentage-error-vs-savin-et-al-2011>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-measurement-cross-species-log-log-power-law-scaling-exponent-alpha-lambda-ell-alpha>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-measurement-cst-membrane-analytic-gradient-vs-central-finite-difference-max-relative-error>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-measurement-fe-mesh-refinement-sensitivity-of-emergent-loop-count-96x5-128x6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-measurement-pitx2-apicobasal-stiffness-gradient-sensitivity-dn-da-at-chick-e12-fe-sheet>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-measurement-surgical-mesentery-ablation-negative-control-tortuosity-epsilon-0-vs-e12-wild-type>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-measurement-universal-dimensionless-wavelength-to-radius-invariant-lambda-r-across-4-vertebrates>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Savin et al. (2011) discrete gut rod coupled to a finite-element (CST, St.Venant-Kirchhoff) dorsal-mesentery membrane with an apicobasal Pitx2 stiffness gradient — MorphoEval overall 80.0/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py` (overall weighted score 80.0/100, down from 92.6 in v2). The single v2 remediation item is closed honestly: the gut rod now shares its nodes with a 760-triangle St.Venant-Kirchhoff membrane mesh of the fan-shaped dorsal mesentery with a mean-preserving apicobasal Pitx2 stiffness field, and loop number, radius and tortuosity emerge from L-BFGS-B minimisation (analytic gradient verified to 8.2e-11 against finite differences); the prescribed-shape target and calibration divisors that produced the v2 near-perfect matches were removed. The honest reduced model over-predicts N (9.81 vs 8.5) and under-predicts R (0.952 vs 1.15 mm) at E12, gives MAPE 19 % / 21 % across E8-E16 and an ontogenetic R exponent of 0.61 instead of 1.0, is not mesh-converged (7.7 %), and cannot select handedness (pure membrane). The BMP2 > WT > Noggin > ablation ordering and the Pitx2-gradient sensitivity emerge without tuning. The provenance re-check downgrades source-traceability: the cross-species table is law-consistent to ~1 % with identical lambda and R exponents (not digitised data), the BMP2/Noggin moduli and tortuosities are not in Nerurkar 2017, the specimen is an adult mammalian photograph, and the Davis 2008 DOI was not verified offline. Five Lean theorems (0 sorrys) cover the strain, cube-law stationarity, annular inertia, Pitx2 mean preservation and mesh Euler characteristic. Overall 80.0/100 (faithfulness 78.9, reproducibility 82.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 327729c8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 82, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 78, Source and data traceability 74, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/gut_looping_differential_growth_comparison.png: rendered output of 2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py at 327729c8, image/png, 972120 B, 2135×1452 px, artifact_sha256 ecc65dee03e0c3a533d95c7271c0e853a30687d6ea5ba5c237d41f3e7f9c41e4 (sha256 ecc65dee03e0c3a533d95c7271c0e853a30687d6ea5ba5c237d41f3e7f9c41e4), spec_fingerprint 6fb7e55e6158cd10ddf94728c17f791e81e999f808f135655cb2a64003d9cc1b. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 6fb7e55e6158cd10ddf94728c17f791e81e999f808f135655cb2a64003d9cc1b; artifact_sha256: ecc65dee03e0c3a533d95c7271c0e853a30687d6ea5ba5c237d41f3e7f9c41e4; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/fe_mesentery_mesh_reference.json=8025ecf7fd54a0ef..., datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/gut_looping_differential_growth_reference.json=f73121bb4140187f..., datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/intestine_mesentery_specimen.jpg=e12fee9ac1fb5f3d..., datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/paper_citations.bib=201f4db588717f47..., datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/scout_manifest.json=0723b42b4d825087...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-gut-looping-differential-growth-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Savin et al. (2011): the midgut loops because the tube grows faster than the dorsal mesentery it is attached to (strain epsilon = (L_t - L_m)/L_m); loop wavelength and radius scale as lambda = 4.55 ell_*, R = 1.68 ell_* with ell_* = (E_t I_t / (E_m h_m))^(1/3); surgically freed tubes uncoil; the collapse holds across chick ontogeny (E8-E16) and across zebra finch, quail, chick and mouse (Fig. 4e-f) | Nerurkar, Mahadevan & Tabin (2017): BMP2 over-expression increases and Noggin decreases the differential strain and the number of loops at E12 | Kurpios et al. (2008), Davis et al. (2008): Pitx2-dependent left-right asymmetric condensation and architecture of the dorsal mesentery set the handedness of looping; reconstructed_in_script: Analytical strain, annular inertia and cube-law predictions; a 96-node discrete rod (axial + second-difference bending energy) sharing its nodes with the gut edge of a 96 x 5 CST St.Venant-Kirchhoff plane-stress membrane mesh of a trapezoidal fan (root fixed, rod ends pinned) with a mean-preserving apicobasal Pitx2 stiffness field; L-BFGS-B relaxation with emergent turning-number loop count, R = 1/<kappa>, contour length per loop and tortuosity for E8-E16, BMP2/WT/Noggin/ablation at E12, a Pitx2-gradient sweep and a mesh-refinement check; the 14-point analytical collapse; chromaticity + DoG segmentation of a vendored mesentery photograph; transfer_boundary: The FE model is a pure membrane (no sheet bending, no left-right rest curvature): looping handedness is NOT selected and the script makes no chirality claim; W_m/L_m = 0.18, root fraction 0.7, nu_m = 0.45 and a_Pitx2 = 0.4 are modelling assumptions flagged in fe_mesentery_mesh_reference.json, not measurements | The emergent morphometrics are unfitted: E12 N = 9.81 vs 8.5, R = 0.952 vs 1.15 mm; E8-E16 MAPE 18.7 % (N) and 21.4 % (R); the ontogenetic log-log slope of R_sim vs ell_* is 0.61 (cube law 1.0); N changes by 7.7 % on 96x5 -> 128x6 refinement | The 14-point cross-species table in gut_looping_differential_growth_reference.json reproduces lambda = 4.55 ell_* and R = 1.68 ell_* to ~1 % with identical log-log slopes for lambda and R, so the r = 0.9999 collapse is a consistency check of the table against the law, not an independent validation against digitised Fig. 4e-f data; does_not_claim: A Kirchhoff rod with twist, a Kirchhoff-Love shell, chirality / handedness selection, mesh-converged loop numbers, measured Pitx2 stiffness gradients, moduli for the BMP2/Noggin conditions traceable to Nerurkar 2017, or an embryonic-chick specimen image (the vendored photograph is an adult mammalian mesentery)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py:1566-1574 with 565-634 — the emergent R exponent across E8-E16 is 0.61 (cube law 1.0) and R is 21 % low / N 19 % high. Diagnose whether this is discretisation (ds_t = 0.72 mm at E12 vs R ~ 1 mm, ~9 rod nodes per loop) or the compression-resisting SVK sheet: re-run E8-E16 at n_s = 192 / n_w = 7 and with a tension-field (compression-free) membrane variant, and report the exponent for each.",
        "remediation needed: 2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py:1766-1786 — the eight physical/mesh CLI overrides reach only render_comparison_figure; render_pitx2_fe_figure and render_growth_gif take only --seed. Thread `overrides` through all three renderers (and the measurements) so --pitx2-grad / --mesh-ns actually change every output.",
        "remediation needed: 2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py:312-339 and 403-414 — the mesentery is a pure SVK membrane with no bending stiffness and no left-right rest curvature, so looping handedness is not selected (the Section 3 header L242-247 says so). Add a discrete Kirchhoff-Love bending term (dihedral-angle hinge energy across each interior edge, stiffness E_m h_m^3 / 12(1 - nu^2)) and a Pitx2-driven leftward rest tilt of the fan (Davis 2008 / Kurpios 2008) so that the writhe sign is reproducible across seeds; assert it in self_test.",
        "remediation needed: 2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py:443-450 and 504 — E8 and E16 reach maxiter 12000 with lbfgs_converged = False and nothing asserts convergence. Either raise maxiter / loosen ftol to a documented gradient-norm criterion and assert `lbfgs_converged` for all 5 stages in self_test, or report the final projected-gradient norm as a measurement.",
        "remediation needed: 2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py:490-511 and 342-365 — rename `lambda_sim_mm` to `contour_per_loop_sim_mm` at the call sites (or compute a true spatial wavelength from the centerline power spectrum) and drop or rename the `relax_kirchhoff_gut_rod` alias; add a twist degree of freedom or stop calling the second-difference rod a Kirchhoff rod in the Section 3 title.",
        "remediation needed: 2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py:678-703 and 1719-1721 — N changes by 7.7 % on 96x5 -> 128x6 and a 96x7 prototype gave N ~ 11.0; the self-test tolerates 20 %. Add a 3-level refinement study (Richardson extrapolation of N and R) and tighten the tolerance to the extrapolated error; include the refined-mesh E12 N and R as measurements with the coarse/fine spread as uncertainty.",
        "remediation needed: 2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py:837-899 and 1626-1634 — the vendored specimen is an adult mammalian mesentery photograph, its lambda/R = 1.54 vs 2.71, the CV references (0.18, 'CV < 0.25') are unsourced and the < 3-peak fallback nn_spacings = [28, 30, 29] is templated. Vendor an embryonic chick midgut image (e.g. a CC-licensed E12 whole-mount), source the CV reference to a figure or drop it, and raise an error instead of substituting spacings.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/gut_looping_differential_growth_reference.json (BMP2 / Noggin rows) and 2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py:781-831 — E_m = 2.35 / 1.25 kPa, h_m = 0.044 / 0.031 mm and tortuosity 5.15 / 2.95 are attributed to Nerurkar 2017 Figs. 2-3, which report strain and loop-number changes, not moduli or tortuosity. Mark these as model assumptions (as the FE JSON does), or source them; drive the BMP2 / Noggin conditions by epsilon alone and report the sensitivity to the assumed E_m / h_m.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/gut_looping_differential_growth_reference.json:151-166 — the cross_species_scaling table reproduces lambda = 4.55 ell_* and R = 1.68 ell_* to ~1 % with identical log-log slopes (0.9909 +/- 0.0027) for lambda and R, i.e. it was generated from the law rather than digitised from Savin Fig. 4e-f. Either replace it with digitised points (with a digitisation note and per-point error bars) or relabel the three 4-species measurements as law-consistency checks and remove 'validation' from their names.",
        "remediation needed: morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_062_gut_looping_differential_growth.lean:101-142 — the Pass 3 theorems are structural (mean preservation, Euler characteristic). Add one statement about the mechanics, e.g. that the discrete bending energy sum_i |r_{i+1} - 2 r_i + r_{i-1}|^2 vanishes iff the rod is straight (collinear equally spaced nodes), matching the ablation invariant asserted at L1683-1685." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Savin et al. (2011) discrete gut rod coupled to a finite-element (CST, St.Venant-Kirchhoff) dorsal-mesentery membrane with an apicobasal Pitx2 stiffness gradient — Parameter expressivity: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The morphospace is now genuinely mechanical: 5 chick stages (L565-634), a 5-point Pitx2 gradient sweep with a = 0 as the uniform-sheet ablation (L637-675), a mesh-refinement pair (L678-703), the 14-point 4-species analytical collapse (L706-778), 4 E12 conditions (L781-831), and CLI overrides --epsilon / --E-ratio / --R-t / --h-m / --pitx2-grad / --width-ratio / --mesh-ns / --mesh-nw / --seed whose defaults are read from the pinned fe_mesentery_mesh_reference.json (L552-562, L1749-1759). Deductions: the eight physical/mesh overrides reach only `render_comparison_figure`; the Pitx2 figure and the GIF ignore everything but --seed (L1780-1786) (-6); W_m/L_m, root fraction and nu_m are swept nowhere in the rendered outputs although the JSON note claims a prototype W_m sweep (-4); the Pitx2 sweep spans only a >= 0 (stiffer toward the gut edge) so the sign of the effect is not exercised (-2); the cross-species morphospace is analytical only (no FE relaxation per species) (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py L1747–L1787: CLI: 8 physical/mesh overrides + --seed; overrides are passed only to render_comparison_figure, not to render_pitx2_fe_figure or render_growth_gif <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py#L1747-L1787>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Savin et al. (2011) discrete gut rod coupled to a finite-element (CST, St.Venant-Kirchhoff) dorsal-mesentery membrane with an apicobasal Pitx2 stiffness gradient — Reproducibility package: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`self_test()` (L1648-1744) runs 13 checks in ~112 s: 5-file SHA-256 integrity, JSON-to-code parity including the new comparison targets, FD gradient exactness (< 1e-5), mesh topology and Euler characteristic, Pitx2 mean preservation, ablation uncoiling, emergent looping at every chick stage with < 50 % error, 4-species collapse, emergent BMP2/WT/Noggin ordering for N and R, monotone Pitx2 sweep, refinement < 20 %, specimen segmentation, and bitwise two-run determinism of the FE solver (L1729-1734); results are cached per parameter key (L366-369) and the default render (~72 s) writes the PNG, the new Pitx2 PNG and a 6-frame GIF. Deductions: `lbfgs_converged` (L504) is recorded but never asserted, and E8 / E16 hit maxiter 12000 with success = False, so the self-test certifies near-stationary rather than converged minima (-4); the 20 % refinement tolerance and 50 % error tolerances are loose enough that the test cannot regress on accuracy (-3); `*.png` is git-ignored repo-wide so the two PNG outputs are not versioned (-2); no requirements lock or MPLCONFIGDIR note accompanies the 112 s / 72 s runtimes, and `measure_morphoeval()` costs ~57 s from a fresh process (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py L1719–L1721: Refinement tolerance 20 % (observed 7.7 %); accuracy tolerances 50 % at L1695-1696 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py#L1719-L1721>",
        "2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py L443–L450: L-BFGS-B with maxiter 12000, ftol 1e-13, gtol 1e-9; opt.success stored at L504 but not asserted anywhere <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py#L443-L450>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-repro-package-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Savin et al. (2011) discrete gut rod coupled to a finite-element (CST, St.Venant-Kirchhoff) dorsal-mesentery membrane with an apicobasal Pitx2 stiffness gradient — Source and data traceability: 74/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Five sources carry DOIs in the script header, the dataset README and `paper_citations.bib`; all 5 dataset files are SHA-256 pinned (L102-119) and verified fail-closed at every run (L133-144); the new `fe_mesentery_mesh_reference.json` separates `mesh_defaults` (labelled modelling assumptions) from `comparison_targets` (arithmetic on the pinned observations) with a `provenance_note` and per-source `used_for` fields. Deductions: the 14-row `cross_species_scaling` table (reference JSON L151-166) reproduces lambda = 4.55 ell_* and R = 1.68 ell_* to ~1 % with the SAME log-log slope 0.9909 +/- 0.0027 for lambda and R and lambda/R CV 0.8 %, which digitised Fig. 4e-f data would not do; its per-row E_t/E_m, h_m and R_i are not traceable to any table in Savin 2011 (-10); the BMP2/Noggin rows carry E_m = 2.35 / 1.25 kPa, h_m = 0.044 / 0.031 mm and tortuosities 5.15 / 2.95 attributed to Nerurkar 2017 Figs. 2-3, which report strain and loop-number changes rather than moduli or tortuosity (-6); the specimen image metadata describes an adult mammalian photograph as the comparison specimen for an embryonic chick model (-4); the Davis 2008 DOI 10.1016/j.devcel.2008.05.001 could not be verified offline (bib note says so) (-2); the 'CV < 0.25' and 0.18 CV references are unsourced (-2); `scout_manifest.json` and the README do not record which figure each chick-stage modulus (E_t, E_m) was digitised from (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py L781–L831: BMP2/Noggin E_m_kPa, h_m_mm and tortuosity_obs taken from the condition table and attributed to Nerurkar 2017, which does not report moduli or tortuosity <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py#L781-L831>",
        "datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/gut_looping_differential_growth_reference.json L151–L166: 14-row cross_species_scaling table: lambda_obs / ell_* = 4.52-4.60 and R_obs / ell_* ~ 1.68 for every row, identical log-log slopes for lambda and R — consistent with generation from the law, not digitisation of Fig. 4e-f <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/gut_looping_differential_growth_reference.json#L151-L166>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-source-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.4e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Savin et al. (2011) discrete gut rod coupled to a finite-element (CST, St.Venant-Kirchhoff) dorsal-mesentery membrane with an apicobasal Pitx2 stiffness gradient — Morphological realism / specimen match: 74/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Judged on the regenerated PNG / GIF and the emergent numbers: Panel A shows a looped rod attached to a stiffness-coloured fan mesh that reads as a mesentery-suspended midgut, Panel F compares emergent N and R to the observed E8-E16 values with the MAPE in the title, the ablation control uncoils to tortuosity 1.000, and the BMP2 > WT > Noggin ordering of N (14.65 / 9.81 / 4.99 vs obs 11.5 / 8.5 / 5.5) and of R (0.80 / 0.95 / 1.35 vs obs 0.98 / 1.15 / 1.40) emerges without tuning. Deductions: the E12 loop count is 15 % high and the radius 17 % low, with E8-E16 MAPE of 19 % and 21 % (-8); the only vendored specimen image is an adult mammalian mesentery photograph from Wikimedia, not an embryonic chick midgut, its segmented lambda/R is 1.54 against the paper's 2.71 (reported at L1642) and the segmentation falls back to a hard-coded spacing triple when fewer than 3 peaks are found (L893-899) (-10); the CV reference 0.18 and 'CV < 0.25' (L1630-1631) are not sourced to any figure of Savin 2011 (-3); the specimen comparison is 2D nearest-neighbour spacing on a photograph, not a morphometric of the rendered 3D loops against embryo images (-5). Credit is given for the honest MAPE labelling in the figure and for the BMP2/Noggin/ablation ordering being emergent." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py L1626–L1644: Specimen CV 0.2319 vs unsourced reference 0.18 / 'CV < 0.25'; specimen lambda/R = 1.54 vs 2.71 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py#L1626-L1644>",
        "2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py L837–L899: Chromaticity + DoG segmentation of an adult mammalian mesentery photograph (not embryonic chick); hard-coded fallback nn_spacings = [28, 30, 29] when < 3 peaks <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py#L837-L899>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-specimen-match-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-specimen-match-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.4e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

